member.example:
Untyped hybrid input — patterns are auto-classified:

var input = new PatternInput(
    patterns: ["**", "!*.log", "important.log"]
);

Mixed typed input — GitIgnore and Regex patterns declared explicitly:

var input = new PatternInput(
    typedPatterns: new Dictionary<PatternKind, IEnumerable<string>>
    {
        [PatternKind.GitIgnore] = ["**", "!*.cs"],
        [PatternKind.Regex]     = ["r:^data_.*\\.log$"]
    }
);

remarks.code:
bool matches = element switch {
    CharLiteral lit  => lit.Value == c,
    CharRange   rng  => c >= rng.Start && c <= rng.End,
    PosixClass  pos  => MatchesPosix(pos.Name, c),
    CharacterClassParseError _ => false,
    _ => false
};
